E={12: 'Glimpses of a ride through the inside of a box with clowns sitting around. The one perpetrator is holding the man’s hand, rubbing his trembling hand like a wife. “Oh… My beautiful darling!” the clown says to the catatonic man, his face wrenching down with heartbreak. The man glimpses this, and looks down at his body, and finds the arm swarming in blue parasites slugging under his skin, before his head rolls down as he passes out a little more again. Phases of human consciousness find his soul in little moments, before his eyes fall shut into black again.', 20: 'The one clown perverted looks over at the man, saying, “Imagine this is a joke. Wouldn’t that be funny, Ouroboros?” His smile now like a friend and brother of all time, the grin shitting a smile eating itself like a dumb relative. “Wouldn’t that be funny!” the clown says again, his snorting and snickers cry out in joyous hoot swings.', 22: 'The immediate burst of laughter escapes the man confined to the stretcher, being able to laugh now, unable to hold the eccentric jazz rhythm of the lungs’ rising and falling chuckles. All the clowns shoot their laughter across the room loudly, dying of joyful pleasure. He laughs even harder, “I hate God!” He looks over at all the clowns, where they all look in knowing of this mutual value. One clown, almost dead, giggles from the ground as through a broken windpipe. As the man strapped down, Ouroboros, laughs, he lets rings in a stifle of lip bite, before saying more, “I fucking hate you, Lucifer!” He cackles more in rolls that can’t escape.', 26: '“Wait,” Lucifer says, his laughs growing a little suspicious now, “Who the fuck are you guys?” he asks of the other clowns.', 28: '“Just words is all, see?” one clown answers, as he points to the outside boundary of their reality, the edge of a papyrus they were all written into. Lucifer and Ouroboros realize they are in the dream of ink and scroll.'}
